    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on a policy draft for our museum board about how we handle artifacts from the colonial era. can u write a quick summary of the main arguments for and against repatriating items to their countries of origin? i need to show both sides of the debate for the memo. thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Arguments for repatriation center on ethical imperatives, asserting that cultural objects belong to their communities of origin and were acquired unethically during colonial periods. Proponents emphasize the importance of decolonizing museum practices and rectifying historical injustices. Conversely, arguments against immediate repatriation often cite issues of preservation capacity in source countries, the complexity of ownership documentation, or the universal museum ideal, which posits that certain artifacts hold global cultural value when housed in major institutions.",
